12. Should we use array index as React key?
Usually no, especially if the list can change.
Bad:
users.map((user, index) => (
  <User key={index} user={user} />
))
Better:
users.map(user => (
  <User key={user.id} user={user} />
))
Why?
React uses keys to identify elements between renders.
Suppose:
A
B
C
Then you insert:
X
A
B
C
With indexes, React sees:
0 → X
1 → A
2 → B
3 → C
The identities shift.
This can cause unexpected behavior, especially when list items contain:
Input fields
Component state
Animations
Editable data
Interview answer
We should prefer a stable unique ID as a key. Index keys are acceptable only for static lists where the order and contents never change.
